Cross-Validation: GSE19188

Independent validation of the GSE18842 differential expression findings using GSE19188, a second NSCLC microarray dataset (91 tumor vs. 65 normal, Affymetrix GPL570 — same platform as GSE18842).

Method
Differential expression run independently on GSE19188 via GEO2R (limma), same thresholds as GSE18842: adj. p-value < 0.05, |log2FC| > 1.5
Upregulated and downregulated gene lists compared against GSE18842's lists for overlap
Overlapping (validated) gene sets carried forward into pathway enrichment (Enrichr: KEGG, MSigDB Hallmark, GO BP)
12-gene clinical biomarker panel checked for correct direction and significance in both datasets

Note: GSE19188's initial GEO2R export had a reversed tumor/normal contrast direction, caught via biological anchor genes (TOP2A/CDK1/CCNB1/MKI67 should be up in tumor; AGER/SFTPC should be down). Fixed by relabeling files and flipping logFC signs before comparison.

Results
Direction	Overlap with GSE18842	% of GSE19188 replicated
Upregulated	328 genes	91.6%
Downregulated	719 genes	84.0%

Biomarker panel: 11/12 validated in the correct direction in both datasets.

Pathway enrichment (validated overlap genes):

Upregulated → Cell cycle, E2F Targets, Mitotic Sister Chromatid Segregation
Downregulated → Cell adhesion molecules, TNF-alpha/NF-kB signaling, Regulation of Angiogenesis
Conclusion

Over 84–91% of GSE19188's significant gene signature was independently replicated in GSE18842, confirming the core NSCLC transcriptomic changes are consistent across patient cohorts rather than dataset-specific artifacts.
